Method add(int index, Object element) overrides ArrayList.add(index, element). It inserts at index shifting elements to the right. The comment: "If the index is within the valid range, then for every element from the index to the old size minus one, the element at the next position is either null if the current element is null, or the element at the next position is equal to the current element."

We need to write assert statement reflecting this property.

We need to refer to old size: \old(this.size()).

Valid index range for add: index >=0 && index <= old size (since insertion allowed at size). In ArrayList, add(index, element) throws IndexOutOfBoundsException if index <0 or > size. So valid range is 0 <= index && index <= oldSize.

The comment says "If the index is within the valid range, then for every element from the index to the old size minus one, the element at the next position is either null if the current element is null, or the element at the next position is equal to the current element."

